{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793519717,"nonce":"BkyM7KU4NNCPyVz8elkzvxVIIUY=","title":"Dogfood canary: a Forgejo repo with scheduled synthetic commits","message":"Owner 2026-11-01: \"for the dog fooding should we also add a forgejo repo and commit and push frequently on it\". Dogfood is staging (owner 2026-11-01); it only gets traffic when someone pushes to this GitHub repo, so on a quiet day it sits idle and drifts unnoticed.\n\nProposal (audit it before building — a new idea, see memory 'audit new ideas before recommending'):\n- `just up dogfood` also seeds a repo on the in-cluster Forgejo (deploy/kind/forgejo.yaml, present in every mode since PR #67), binds it through a Forgejo connection, and applies a Kubernetes CronJob that commits through the Forgejo contents API every 20–30 min (bounded: colima is 2 vCPU / 4 GiB; the stack budget is ~2 GiB excluding step workloads). Delivery is in-cluster (Forgejo → server Service), no tunnel.\n- The canary repo's pipeline covers what this repo's own CI does not: a library invoke, results + artifacts, a manual gate (auto-released or left pending on purpose), a matrix, and a step that fails on a seeded fraction of commits so retries, Reruns and Takes happen. Steps stay busybox-sized.\n- Long-running checks it should make visible: memory growth (server, Depot), Postgres and MinIO growth with retention on, Depot cache eviction, lease renewal, readoption after `just reload`.\n\nKnown limit: the in-cluster Forgejo is plain HTTP, so canary pipelines cannot use lib:thulasi-ram/clone with forge_token (Scarab refuses to mint for a non-https clone URL, and the pinned clone image's askpass refuses too). Forge-token coverage stays in `just e2e` (quick tunnel) and in GitHub dogfood.\n\nCosts: a few Pods per interval while dogfood is up; DB/bucket growth (needs retention in dogfood values); canary Runs in the UI (own Project, filterable).\n\nAcceptance: after `just up dogfood`, a canary Run appears at least every 30 min without anyone pushing; a day-long soak shows node memory and DB/bucket size bounded (numbers recorded); `just down` removes the CronJob; no new top-level just recipe (see c043abf).","files":null}]}